# Scope for `semgrep ci` / `semgrep scan`. Anchored paths are repo-root
# relative (gitignore syntax) — keep the leading `/` so they cannot match
# a same-named directory deeper in the tree.
#
# Rationale: the untrusted boundary (MCP tool args, CLI input) is guarded by
# resolveKbPath/resolveKnowledgeBaseDir/assertNoTraversal in src/kb-fs.ts,
# so audit rules firing on path.join/path.resolve elsewhere are noise. The
# real attack surface left scanned: src/, .github/, package-lock.json.

# Dev-only benchmark tooling (python/ts corpus runners, mlflow, adjudication):
# child_process, weak-hash, and non-literal-regexp findings here are all in
# operator-driven scripts that never see untrusted input.
/benchmarks/

# Repo-local generator/dev scripts (.mjs) — same operator-only trust level.
/scripts/

# Test harnesses and scenarios — spawn/eval in test scaffolding is expected.
/tests/

# Deliberately planted fixture secrets (JWT/AWS/GitHub tokens) used by the
# redaction + secret-scanner test corpus — always false positives.
/src/test-support/

# Unit/integration/e2e test files at any depth — intentional secrets,
# spawnShell calls, and path fixtures live here by design.
*.test.ts
*.test.js
*.test.mjs
